<title>INDIA: Abu Dhabi Commercial bank cuts Indain prime rate.</title>
<headline>Abu Dhabi Commercial bank cuts Indain prime rate.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Abu Dhabi Commercial Bank will cut its Indian prime lending rate to 16.0 percent per annum from 17.5 percent effective May 1, a bank official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The maximum spread over the prime rate will be four percentage points, he said.</p>
<p>The rate cut follows measures announced by the Reserve Bank of India to reduce deposit rates in its monetary policy for the first half of financial year 1997/98 (April-March), released on April 15.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
